<title>SWEDEN: Scania posts 44 pct drop in '96 profits.</title>
<headline>Scania posts 44 pct drop in '96 profits.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bus and truck maker Scania</p>
<p>reports for the 12 months to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  2,706 vs   4,847</p>
<p> Sales total				33,730 vs  34,840</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	    5.50  vs    5.50</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		9.90  vs   16.40</p>
<p> Manufacturing, sale, admin costs   29,700 vs  28,793</p>
<p> Other income and expenses		  55 vs	98</p>
<p> Operating profit before deprec	4,085 vs   6,145</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,328 vs   1,136</p>
<p> Associate interests			 300 vs     343</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	 3,057 vs   5,352</p>
<p> Net financial items			 351 vs     505</p>
<p> Taxes					   725 vs   1,566</p>
<p> Minorities					0 vs	 1</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,981 vs   3,280</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll of 16 analysts found market expectations for Scania to report a profit after financial items of 2.76 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
